ring the  1968 prague spring and these tribes  themselves are used to differentiate  between  enemy and friendly vehicles of course  meanwhile certain russian officials are  openly threatening ukraine with invasion  putin has not threatened ukraine yet at  least not openly  but i mean the writing is pretty much on  the wall at this point  the argument right now is the same as  ever that russia needs to protect  russian citizens abroad meanwhile the  reason why  there are russians in donbass is because  russia gave out a bunch of russian  passports to the local ukrainians  which is basically giving them  citizenship so i guess that's one way to  have  russians abroad that need protecting but  of course the protection  of russian citizens is not the real  reason i mean you have to be a complete  tool to believe that  you know since when does the russian  government care about its people  they're exporting sputnik 5 vaccines all  around the world to get  geopolitical clouts meanwhile they don't  have enough to vaccinate the domestic  population  so yeah that's how much they care about  russian citizens when it's not  politically opportune to do so  and russia and putin in general is kind  of  in trouble right now the covet epidemic  has hit the russian economy pretty hard  meanwhile we have of course  unprecedented corruption in government  you know obnoxious enrichment for the  ruling class  and general poverty for the rest of the  people basically  uh lower salaries uh falling living  standards  it's not so nice to live there right now  and accordingly putin's approval ratings  are  pretty low it is currently slogging  around  65 percent which would be pretty high in  a democracy  but if you consider that putin's  approval rating after crimea was taken  over  was 89 like that man had a mandate  this is now pretty much gone as the  military successes  afterglow kind of fades and economic  problems compound  so basically right now putin needs  another patriotic war to 